    "fix": "Extend the pyo3 exports to take the same parameter blocks the WASM ones do. Until then a placement on a studio-authored world is not reproducible in Python, and this file records that rather than hiding it.",
    "why": "The Python surface - oracle and pyo3 wheel alike - takes only seed, radius, plate_count and land_fraction. The opt-in tectonic, coast and gully parameters are exposed through the WASM exports only, so a Python placement on this world builds a DIFFERENT planet. It put these rooms at -406 m; the real ground is -0.14 to +2.2 m, an error of four hundred metres."
  },
